{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1329 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "98b2ebe06601bb99ce656694ae3e3da5475ba8d925e457f57ccdf2440b6d4793" :edb/db-before-t 1328 :edb/db-after-t 1329 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534641 50 #inst "2026-10-08T03:04:07.146Z" 13194139534641 true] [17592186157072 1100 "Solve the inequality $\\dfrac{(x^2-8)^3}{11^x} \\geq 0$." 13194139534641 false] [17592186157072 1100 "Solve the inequality $\\dfrac{(x^2-8)^3}{11^x} \\geq 0.$" 13194139534641 true] [17592186157072 1145 "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nMultiplying both sides of the given inequality by $11^x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}((x^{2} - 8)^{3})/(11^{x}) & \\ge 0 \\\\ 11^{x} \\cdot ((x^{2} - 8)^{3})/(11^{x}) & \\ge 11^{x} \\cdot 0 \\\\ (x^{2} - 8)^{3} & \\ge 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{(x^{2} - 8)^{3}}\\begin{vmatrix}\\ge \\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ x^{2} - 8\\end{vmatrix}\\ge 0; x^{2}\\begin{vmatrix}\\ge 8 \\\\ \\sqrt{x^{2}}\\end{vmatrix}\\ge \\sqrt{8}; \\mid x \\mid \\mid \\ge 2\\sqrt{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is\n\n$$\nx \\leq -2\\sqrt 2\n$$\n\nor\n\n$$\nx \\geq 2 \\sqrt 2\n$$" 13194139534641 false] [17592186157072 1145 "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nMultiplying both sides of the given inequality by $11^x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{({x}^{2}-8)^{3}}{{11}^{x}} & \\ge 0 \\\\ {11}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{({x}^{2}-8)^{3}}{{11}^{x}} & \\ge {11}^{x}\\cdot 0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-8)^{3} & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{({x}^{2}-8)^{3}} & \\ge \\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ {x}^{2}-8 & \\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\ge 8 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\ge \\sqrt{8} \\\\ |x| & \\ge 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $x \\leq -2\\sqrt 2$ or $x \\geq 2 \\sqrt 2.$" 13194139534641 true] [17592186157073 1100 "Solve the inequality $x^2e^{x+1}-2e^{x+1} < -xe^{x+1} .$" 13194139534641 true] [17592186157073 1100 "Solve the inequality $x^2e^{x+1}-2e^{x+1} < -xe^{x+1}$." 13194139534641 false] [17592186157073 1145 "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{e}^{x+1}-2{e}^{x+1} & <-x{e}^{x+1} \\\\ {x}^{2}{e}^{x+1}+x{e}^{x+1}-2{e}^{x+1} & <0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+x-2){e}^{x+1} & <0 \\\\ (x+2)(x-1){e}^{x+1} & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by $e^{x+1}$ and get\n\n$$\n(x+2)(x-1) <   0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-2$ and $x=1.$ The parabola is below the $x$-axis when $-2 <   x <   1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/2f01104ae0cb9a41c5c5e4b8393e346f7d0e9b2bfd1afa593ee6bdfb0fff39f2.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-2 <   x <   1.$" 13194139534641 true] [17592186157073 1145 "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x^{2}e^{x + 1} - 2e^{x + 1} & < - xe^{x + 1} \\\\ x^{2}e^{x + 1} + xe^{x + 1} - 2e^{x + 1} & < 0 \\\\ (x^{2} + x - 2)e^{x + 1} & < 0 \\\\ (x + 2)(x - 1)e^{x + 1} & < 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by $e^{x+1}$ and get\n\n$$\n(x+2)(x-1) < 0\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-2$ and $x=1$. The parabola is below the $x$-axis when $-2 < x < 1$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2859/Source/Images/9bc30ffe9a0c96ace6cb684a3dbd1068.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-2 < x < 1$." 13194139534641 false] [17592186157074 1100 "Solve the inequality $x^5 \\cdot 4^{x} > 4^{x - 15}$." 13194139534641 false] [17592186157074 1100 "Solve the inequality $x^5 \\cdot 4^{x} > 4^{x - 15}.$" 13194139534641 true] [17592186157074 1145 "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{x} & >{4}^{x-15} \\\\ {x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{x}-{4}^{x-15} & >0 \\\\ ({x}^{5}-{4}^{-15})\\cdot {4}^{x} & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by $4^{x}$ and get\n\n$$\nx^5 - 4^{-15} > 0.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5} & >{4}^{-15} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{5}} & >\\sqrt[5]{{4}^{-15}} \\\\ x & >{({4}^{-15})}^{1/5} \\\\ x & >{4}^{-3} \\\\ x & >\\frac{1}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $x > \\dfrac{1}{64}.$" 13194139534641 true] [17592186157074 1145 "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x^{5} \\cdot 4^{x} & > 4^{x - 15} \\\\ x^{5} \\cdot 4^{x} - 4^{x - 15} & > 0 \\\\ (x^{5} - 4^{-15}) \\cdot 4^{x} & > 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by $4^{x}$ and get\n\n$$\nx^5 - 4^{-15} > 0\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x^{5} & > 4^{-15} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{x^{5}} & > \\sqrt[5]{4^{-15}} \\\\ x & > (4^{-15})^{1/5} \\\\ x & > 4^{-3} \\\\ x & > \\frac{1}{64}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is\n\n$$\nx > \\dfrac{1}{64}\n$$" 13194139534641 false] [17592186157261 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300620 13194139534641 true] [17592186157261 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300627 13194139534641 true] [17592186157261 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300634 13194139534641 true] [17592186157261 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300683 13194139534641 true] [17592186157261 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300691 13194139534641 true] [17592186157262 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300641 13194139534641 true] [17592186157262 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300648 13194139534641 true] [17592186157262 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300676 13194139534641 true] [17592186157262 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300698 13194139534641 true] [17592186157262 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300704 13194139534641 true] [17592186157263 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300655 13194139534641 true] [17592186157263 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300662 13194139534641 true] [17592186157263 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300669 13194139534641 true] [17592186157263 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300711 13194139534641 true] [17592186157851 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534641 true] [17592186157851 1100 "Solve the inequality $3^{4x}x^{2} \\ge 3^{4x + 1}x$." 13194139534641 false] [17592186157851 1100 "Solve the inequality ${3}^{4x}{x}^{2}\\ge {3}^{4x+1}x.$" 13194139534641 true] [17592186157851 1145 "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{4x}{x}^{2} & \\ge {3}^{4x+1}x \\\\ {3}^{4x}{x}^{2}-{3}^{4x+1}x & \\ge 0 \\\\ {3}^{4x}({x}^{2}-3x) & \\ge 0 \\\\ {3}^{4x}x(x-3) & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${3}^{4x}$ and get\n\n$$\nx(x-3)\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=0$ and $x=3.$ The parabola is at or above the $x$-axis when $x\\le 0$ or $x\\ge 3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/3bfb82543e7c05d0ca0b8f6c6973025400ad1253acbc57214173dbd3e8c37fef.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is  $x\\le 0$ or $x\\ge 3.$" 13194139534641 true] [17592186300620 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300621 13194139534641 true] [17592186300620 1089 "q-115404" 13194139534641 true] [17592186300620 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534641 true] [17592186300620 1100 "Solve the inequality $(4{x}^{6}+3)\\cdot (0.33)^{2x-5}\\ge 0.$" 13194139534641 true] [17592186300620 1113 #uuid "2f6ef83f-0afe-5013-adb1-85c6601a8666" 13194139534641 true] [17592186300620 1145 "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nDividing both sides of the given inequality by $(0.33)^{2x-5},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4{x}^{6}+3)\\cdot (0.33)^{2x-5} & \\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{(4{x}^{6}+3)\\cdot (0.33)^{2x-5}}{(0.33)^{2x-5}} & \\ge \\frac{0}{(0.33)^{2x-5}} \\\\ 4{x}^{6}+3 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFurthermore, $4{x}^{6}+3\\ge 0$ for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the solution is all real numbers." 13194139534641 true] [17592186300621 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300622 13194139534641 true] [17592186300621 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300623 13194139534641 true] [17592186300621 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300624 13194139534641 true] [17592186300621 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300625 13194139534641 true] [17592186300621 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300626 13194139534641 true] [17592186300621 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534641 true] [17592186300621 1041 "selection" 13194139534641 true] [17592186300621 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300623 13194139534641 true] [17592186300621 1110 #uuid "1350abaa-be9e-5288-b428-4417f3430e7a" 13194139534641 true] [17592186300622 1034 "x\\ge 0" 13194139534641 true] [17592186300622 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534641 true] [17592186300622 1111 #uuid "5dadc738-d4d0-597e-ac4c-f9a561e8fceb" 13194139534641 true] [17592186300623 1034 "all real numbers" 13194139534641 true] [17592186300623 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534641 true] [17592186300623 1111 #uuid "846d1070-81b9-593e-af5c-2c18ab33cc63" 13194139534641 true] [17592186300624 1034 "x\\ge \\frac{4}{3}" 13194139534641 true] [17592186300624 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534641 true] [17592186300624 1111 #uuid "04197ece-15d0-5cff-916b-3a3bb8d4093f" 13194139534641 true] [17592186300625 1034 "no solutions" 13194139534641 true] [17592186300625 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534641 true] [17592186300625 1111 #uuid "34d1d205-798a-52d6-a246-86c00e9d0375" 13194139534641 true] [17592186300626 1034 "x\\ge \\frac{1}{3}" 13194139534641 true] [17592186300626 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534641 true] [17592186300626 1111 #uuid "b5809cd6-a6be-5e5d-a775-7e24437d8391" 13194139534641 true] [17592186300627 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300628 13194139534641 true] [17592186300627 1089 "q-115408" 13194139534641 true] [17592186